[{:db/id 17592186059707 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-806aafe6-aa9d-53f3-a7d9-19809d388a29" "question-55e540af-11e2-5ec3-9b47-ab0da3ac740e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-806aafe6-aa9d-53f3-a7d9-19809d388a29" :question/id #uuid "806aafe6-aa9d-53f3-a7d9-19809d388a29" :question/math-academy-id "q-82092" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- **If** $7$ is an even number, **then** $6$ is an odd number.\n- **If** $6$ is an even number, **then** $7$ is an even number.\n- **If** $6$ is an even number, **then** $7$ is an odd number." :question/worked-solution "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is true. The antecedent \"$7$ is an even number\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement II is false. The antecedent \"$6$ is an even number\" is true, and the consequent \"$7$ is an even number\" is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement III is true. The antecedent \"$6$ is an even number\" is true, and the consequent \"$7$ is an odd number\" is true. So the promise is kept, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1cad3447-1622-501b-827e-837284b22076"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1cad3447-1622-501b-827e-837284b22076" :answer-field/id #uuid "1cad3447-1622-501b-827e-837284b22076" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-383d59b8-a864-5389-8975-dc9bbacfa5e6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-383d59b8-a864-5389-8975-dc9bbacfa5e6" "answer-ac3fcded-1928-518d-b875-ec2601c5af9f" "answer-9ca16a39-9404-5469-a817-d4f31a93d630" "answer-2c24a347-5951-5876-9f2d-8a1d7c5b9f75" "answer-5017cc1a-c69b-5371-9aff-5e273c1bbfe5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-383d59b8-a864-5389-8975-dc9bbacfa5e6" :answer/id #uuid "383d59b8-a864-5389-8975-dc9bbacfa5e6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac3fcded-1928-518d-b875-ec2601c5af9f" :answer/id #uuid "ac3fcded-1928-518d-b875-ec2601c5af9f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ca16a39-9404-5469-a817-d4f31a93d630" :answer/id #uuid "9ca16a39-9404-5469-a817-d4f31a93d630" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c24a347-5951-5876-9f2d-8a1d7c5b9f75" :answer/id #uuid "2c24a347-5951-5876-9f2d-8a1d7c5b9f75" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5017cc1a-c69b-5371-9aff-5e273c1bbfe5" :answer/id #uuid "5017cc1a-c69b-5371-9aff-5e273c1bbfe5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-55e540af-11e2-5ec3-9b47-ab0da3ac740e" :question/id #uuid "55e540af-11e2-5ec3-9b47-ab0da3ac740e" :question/math-academy-id "q-103558" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- **If** $12$ is divisible by $3$, **then** $9$ is divisible by $4.$\n- **If** $5$ is divisible by $2$, **then** $10$ is divisible by $5.$\n- **If** $9$ is divisible by $5$, **then** $6$ is divisible by $3.$" :question/worked-solution "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is false. The antecedent \"$12$ is divisible by $3$\" is true, and the consequent \"$9$ is divisible by $4$\" is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement II is true. The antecedent \"$5$ is divisible by $2$\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement III is true. Again, the antecedent \"$9$ is divisible by $5$\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6a77f2d5-b26b-5d52-b3a8-7c324acb6f02"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6a77f2d5-b26b-5d52-b3a8-7c324acb6f02" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a77f2d5-b26b-5d52-b3a8-7c324acb6f02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6faeed3c-4f73-5576-a69a-7f5fc255a52b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6468d182-e5ca-52c7-91c5-873befcae9ce" "answer-96783f0b-1578-5947-bf81-9015eff667e3" "answer-5cfbb4fe-6765-539a-b1fe-a3a402299b48" "answer-6faeed3c-4f73-5576-a69a-7f5fc255a52b" "answer-f2c65aaf-1f1f-5a46-a0a8-cb5ff99c1cc1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6468d182-e5ca-52c7-91c5-873befcae9ce" :answer/id #uuid "6468d182-e5ca-52c7-91c5-873befcae9ce" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96783f0b-1578-5947-bf81-9015eff667e3" :answer/id #uuid "96783f0b-1578-5947-bf81-9015eff667e3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5cfbb4fe-6765-539a-b1fe-a3a402299b48" :answer/id #uuid "5cfbb4fe-6765-539a-b1fe-a3a402299b48" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6faeed3c-4f73-5576-a69a-7f5fc255a52b" :answer/id #uuid "6faeed3c-4f73-5576-a69a-7f5fc255a52b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2c65aaf-1f1f-5a46-a0a8-cb5ff99c1cc1" :answer/id #uuid "f2c65aaf-1f1f-5a46-a0a8-cb5ff99c1cc1" :answer/type :answer.type